{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","record":{"id":"lean.value_consequences","kind":"declaration","label":"OAI.SKValue.value_consequences","status":"unverified","source_id":"scalar_value_proof","statement":"OAI.SKValue.value_consequences is the three-part universally quantified conjunction specified by ComparatorChallenges.SKValue, implemented from scalar_value_target, finite_gaussian_target, and ground_state_parisi_target.","assumption_ids":["assumptions.value_minimizer","assumptions.value_diffusion"],"evidence_ids":["source_bytes_verified","lean_build_not_run","lean_dependencies_not_run","manuscript_alignment_not_run","scalar_value_comparator_not_run","scalar_value_solution_build_failure_20261024","scalar_value_corrected_build_not_run_20261024","scalar_value_corrected_comparator_not_run_20261024","current_input_identity_20261024","corrected_comparator_outcome_unavailable_20261025","corrected_extraction_outcome_unavailable_20261025"],"citation_ids":["scalar_value_implementation","scalar_value_type","scalar_value_comparator"],"boundary":"The first two conjuncts are conditional on IsMinimizer and IsDiffusion; the final Parisi-value equality needs IsMinimizer. These are scalar ground-state value and finite Gaussian approximation statements. They do not assert QAOA circuit-energy convergence or an efficient angle-selection algorithm.","locator":"theorem value_consequences, line 16","declaration":"OAI.SKValue.value_consequences"},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["mapped_claim"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/verification","anchor":"verification","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"},{"stage":"short","passage_ref":"sha256:7b07c474e9e4b493474081a793473deb1d5ecae2fdcc29bf9c00dc4caa8bbe8a/papers/short.md/sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/passages/evidence-scope","anchor":"evidence-scope","mapping_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"},{"stage":"expository","passage_ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/passages/source-record","anchor":"source-record","mapping_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/verification","anchor":"verification","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\nThe source collection retains the two manuscripts, formal statements,\ntheir implementations and build metadata. The derived project specifies\nLean 4.34.1 and a pinned mathlib revision. The proof-assistant and library\ninfrastructure is described by [de Moura and Ullrich (2021), *The Lean 4\nTheorem Prover and Programming Language*](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-79876-5_37)\nand [The mathlib Community (2020), *The Lean Mathematical Library*](https://doi.org/10.1145/3372885.3373824).\nThese references credit the software; the retained project metadata identifies\nthe versions used for this source. The retained polynomial computation\nin §4 uses exact rational arithmetic. Its expansion matches\nall 22 positive remainder\ncoefficients. The surplus of the $v^4$ coefficient above $1/1000$ is\n$140507/1521000000$. This finite check does not establish the PDE\nsigns, integrability, boundary flux or limiting argument.\n\nThe source-byte audit verified the inspected edition; it did not prove\nits claims. Paper assembly checked identifiers, declared scope and\ndocument bindings, not semantic correspondence or reader understanding.\nTool-compatibility checks and synthetic fixtures exercised their stated\ncases, not either selected SK theorem. Reading of the mathematical and\nformal sources supports the bounded comparisons reported here, without\na complete independent proof acceptance or transitive axiom audit.\n\nThe retained observations must be kept separate. The original graph records\nunrun plans and an earlier full-support attempt that could not start\nbecause the Comparator executable was unavailable. A later retained\nattempt, observed on 23 October 2026, built and exported the challenge,\nthen stopped while building the implementing solution. The retained\npartial-observation receipt and log preserve that event: the imported\nobject for `Diffusion/AbsIncrement` was missing. The challenge is an\nadmitted specification, so its successful build and export are not a\nproof of the theorem. There was no successful solution export or\nresearch-target comparison in that observation.\n\nThe scalar-value invocation in the same original two-target run reached\na terminal failure observed on 24 October 2026. Its challenge built and\nexported, but its solution build stopped because the imported object for\n`Gaussian/IntegralPositiveMulGaussian` was missing. The retained scalar\nreceipt and log establish no solution export, kernel acceptance or\ncomparison acceptance. The companion source review locates both records.\nBoth failures concern the original build configuration. A subsequent\nrepair to the derived configuration was recorded. In the subsequent\ncorrected replay, the full-support challenge built and its exporter was\nobserved running. Reconciliation on 25 October found that the controller\nhad stopped without a recovered terminal research result. Comparator\nand research extraction outcomes therefore remain unknown, neither\nrejected nor accepted. The companion source review retains this\ninterruption separately from the original build failures.\n\nThe later observation is additional run history, not a replacement for\nthe earlier event or a mathematical rejection of the theorem. Neither\nresearch target has a successful source-bound comparison and transitive\naxiom audit established here. Permitted axioms and checker settings\ndescribe configuration; source names and tool-fixture receipts cannot\nsupply the missing target result. The full-support receipt remains a\nhistorical partial observation; the scalar receipt is a terminal failure\nof its original invocation. Neither is a replay of the subsequently\nrepaired source configuration.\n\nThis editorial revision does not establish a new formal result.\nDetailed reading coverage, exact finite-check\nresults, preserved unsuccessful observations and the remaining obligations\nare recorded in the companion source review. This remains a draft after source-based agent review; independent mathematical acceptance and a human reconstruction study have not been performed.\n","span":{"start_byte":237289,"end_byte":241317,"start_line":5092,"end_line":5154},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=verification","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=verification"},{"stage":"short","passage_ref":"sha256:7b07c474e9e4b493474081a793473deb1d5ecae2fdcc29bf9c00dc4caa8bbe8a/papers/short.md/sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/passages/evidence-scope","anchor":"evidence-scope","mapping_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\nThis AI-assisted article reconstructs the cited analytic arguments.\nThe integrated estimate (5), its shape hypotheses and compact-strip\napproximation are substantial imported inputs.\n\nThe [full-support formal statement][support-challenge]\nasserts the support and moment conclusions conditional on an admissible\nminimiser, and constructs its associated diffusion. A separate\n[scalar formal statement][value-challenge] covers value identities and\nfinite Gaussian approximation, with minimiser and diffusion premises\nfor those clauses. Its third clause identifies the ground-state and\nParisi values from a minimiser, constructing the diffusion internally.\nThe two formal models have not been transported\ninto one another in this record. Neither statement includes the\npositive-density corollary or QAOA convergence. Their\n[full-support][support-lean] and [scalar][value-lean] implementations\nuse [Lean][Lean4] and [mathlib][mathlib].\n\nAcceptance by Comparator and extraction of the selected formal\nstatements remain unknown. Source inspection alone establishes neither.\nExact versions, checking outcomes and correspondence are retained in the\nlong record's <span class=\"pdf-companion\" data-pdf-target=\"../long/reasoning-record.pdf\" data-pdf-anchor=\"formal-interfaces\">[§12, “What the formal statements establish”](../long/reasoning-record.md#formal-interfaces)</span> and <span class=\"pdf-companion\" data-pdf-target=\"../long/reasoning-record.pdf\" data-pdf-anchor=\"verification\">[§13, “Source checks and finite calculation”](../long/reasoning-record.md#verification)</span>.\n","span":{"start_byte":45434,"end_byte":47016,"start_line":947,"end_line":968},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/short?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=evidence-scope","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=evidence-scope"},{"stage":"expository","passage_ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/passages/source-record","anchor":"source-record","mapping_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n## Sources and scope of verification\n\nThis account reconstructs selected parts of OpenAI's analytic manuscript.\nThe global scaling argument for contact follows Chen's variational proof;\nthe terminal convexity argument in Section 5.4 is an ordinary deduction\nfrom the stated curvature, contact and boundedness inputs. It is not a\nclaim that this alternative proof has been replayed in Lean.\nThe Lean [implementation][support-proof],\n[challenge statement][support-interface] and [Comparator configuration][support-config]\nconcern a minimiser's support and moment identities. They assume a\nminimiser; they do not prove the external Parisi formula or attainment.\nThe separate scalar [implementation][value-proof] and [statement][value-interface]\nconcern the value identity and finite Gaussian approximation. Neither\nselected statement covers positive density, the external near-ground\noverlap theorem used in Section 6, or the complete QAOA circuit theorem.\nThe implementations use [Lean 4 (de Moura–Ullrich, 2021)](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-79876-5_37)\nand [mathlib (The mathlib Community, 2020)](https://doi.org/10.1145/3372885.3373824).\n\nComparator acceptance and research-v2 extraction remain unknown; see the\n*Long Reasoning Record*, <span class=\"pdf-companion\" data-pdf-target=\"../long/reasoning-record.pdf\" data-pdf-anchor=\"verification\">[§13](../long/reasoning-record.md#verification)</span>. Kernel checking establishes a declared statement\nunder its definitions and axioms. Its correspondence with the analytic theorem,\nindependent proof review and reader comprehension are separate questions.\nThe links below select the editions used.\n\n- **OpenAI (2026a).** *Full support of the zero-temperature\n  Sherrington–Kirkpatrick order parameter*, 27 September 2026.\n  [Pinned manuscript][support-manuscript]. §2 supplies regularity,\n  Proposition 5.1 the strict curvature estimate, §6 the support proof,\n  and Corollary 6.4 the additional density conclusion.\n- **Hong-Bin Chen (2026).** *FRSB in the SK spin glass: convergence to full-interval\n  support at zero temperature*. [Version 1][chen-support],\n  Theorem 1.3 for earlier full support and smooth nonnegative density;\n  Proposition 3.2 for contact by scaling the coefficient. Strictly positive\n  density in the further-reading note uses the separate OpenAI corollary.\n- **Antonio Auffinger and Wei-Kuo Chen (2017).** *Parisi formula for\n  the ground state energy in the mixed p-spin model*, Annals of\n  Probability 45(6B), 4617–4631. [Version 2][auffinger-chen].\n  The variational formula and attainment used in Section 3.2.\n- **Aukosh Jagannath and Ian Tobasco (2016).** *A dynamic programming\n  approach to the Parisi functional*, Proceedings of the American\n  Mathematical Society 144, 3135–3150. [Version 4][jt-control].\n  The control method, with finite-temperature terminal data; it is not\n  by itself the zero-temperature regularity theorem used here.\n- **Wei-Kuo Chen, Madeline Handschy and Gilad Lerman (2018).** *On the\n  energy landscape of the mixed even p-spin model*, Probability Theory\n  and Related Fields 171, 53–95. [Version 4][chl-optimality].\n  Proposition 4 gives the first-variation formula used in Section 5.1;\n  the proof of Theorem 6 gives the zero-candidate descent.\n- **Antonio Auffinger, Wei-Kuo Chen and Qiang Zeng (2020).** *The SK model\n  is infinite step replica symmetry breaking at zero temperature*.\n  [Version 2][acz], Proposition 1 and Remark 7. Near-ground overlap pairs\n  and the earlier terminal-plateau observation.\n- **OpenAI (2026b).** *QAOA attains the SK ground-state energy in the\n  thermodynamic-first limit*, 25 September 2026.\n  [Pinned manuscript][qaoa-manuscript]. The separate circuit theorem.\n- **Joao Basso, Edward Farhi, Kunal Marwaha, Benjamin Villalonga and\n  Leo Zhou (2022).** *The Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm\n  at High Depth for MaxCut on Large-Girth Regular Graphs and the\n  Sherrington-Kirkpatrick Model*. [Full preprint, version 3][bfmvz],\n  §7, equation (7.2). The eventual-optimality conjecture.\n","span":{"start_byte":54490,"end_byte":58545,"start_line":1277,"end_line":1337},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/expository?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=expository&passage=source-record","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=expository&passage=source-record"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=lean.value_consequences&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=lean.value_consequences&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=lean.value_consequences&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=lean.value_consequences&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:c6e14b3ed6f19faddcdebafa60d23ad3ca746fc182e385afd3d2000935fc4a00","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/assumptions.value_diffusion","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"field:c80f7cc74e5513a1f3d6d3b9342c76f4507e53138ff1922dacaa2970baaae667","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/assumptions.value_minimizer","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/lean.value_consequences","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efc